<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16343" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσπαίρω</span></b> , impf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤσπαιρον,</span>
		
			Ion.
		 and 
			Ep.
		
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσπαίρεσκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Q.S.
					11.104
				</span></i>
			: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ-</span> euph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπαίρω</span>):—<i>pant, gasp,
				struggle,</i> in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always of the dying (so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κραδίη
				ἀσπαίρουσα</span> must be taken, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				13.443
			</span></i>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ δουρὶ ἤσπαιρ᾽ ὡς ὅτε
				βοῦς κτλ.</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				571
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζωὸν ἔτ᾽ ἀσπαίροντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					12.203
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				19.229
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				977
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				1587
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεκροὶ -οντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					2.4.5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἄνω κάτω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					843
				</span></i>
			; of an infant, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.111
			</span></i>; of fish taken out of the water, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				9.120
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Babr.
				6.5
			</span></i>:—but in <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.5
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀδείμαντος ἤσπαιρε μοῦνος</span> was
			the only one who still <i>made a struggle, resisted</i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐβόων τε καὶ ἤσπαιρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					7.25
				</span></i>
			.—Poet. and 
				Ion.
			 word.</div>
